          "english": "It's best to think of an accent as a distinct, systematic and rule-governed way of speaking. Accent is not a __(26)__ for dialect, but it's related. Dialect is an umbrella term for the way a community pronounces words, creates words, and orders words; accent refers to that first part only.",
