          "english": "Morgan sold the patent to General Electric — and the spread of the traffic light was green lighted. Green means go. It is that simple, but it's still best to check both ways for oncoming traffic that may not be paying attention or is running the light. Yellow means slow down and prepare to stop. It does not mean full-throttle(全速) ahead. While you may get away with gunning it into the intersection, running a yellow can lead to tickets and dangerous accidents. Red lights are a clear and consistent warning to stop. Even where right turns are allowed on red lights, you must come to a complete stop before turning right. You must also yield to any through traffic, which has the right of way. In most states and cities, you can take a right on red unless otherwise indicated. New York City does not allow a right on red.",
          "chinese": "摩根将专利卖给了通用电气公司，交通信号灯的普及也因此获得了绿灯。绿灯表示通行。道理很简单，但你仍然最好向两边查看，因为迎面而来的车辆可能没有注意信号灯，或者正在闯灯。黄灯表示减速并准备停车，并不意味着可以全速前进。虽然你可能侥幸加速驶入十字路口而不被追究，但闯黄灯可能会导致罚单和危险事故。红灯是明确而统一的停车警告。即使红灯时允许右转，右转前也必须完全停车。你还必须让行所有直行车辆，因为它们拥有先行权。在大多数州和城市，除非另有标示，红灯时可以右转。纽约市不允许红灯时右转。",
